  "reply": "`parseDuration` in `src/duration.ts` now accepts one or more components in strictly descending `h`, `m`, `s`, `ms` order, and `bun test` passes (26 tests, 0 failures). I changed only that file.\n\n- **Whitespace:** It is allowed between components and at both ends, but not inside a component, so `1 h` is rejected.\n- **Rejected input:** Empty input, duplicate or out-of-order units, signs, fractions and junk all throw `RangeError`. The whole string must parse, so a partial match never succeeds.\n- **Size limit:** I sum in `BigInt` so the check against `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` is exact. Any single value or total above it throws `RangeError`.\n- **API:** The `parseDuration(text: string): number` export is unchanged.",
